     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p10-definitions-block-p18-definition-text",
     "replacement": "$x$**-intercept:** the point where the line meets the $x$-axis, where $y=0$. Its $x$-coordinate is also called the $x$-intercept.\n\n$y$**-intercept:** the point where the line meets the $y$-axis, where $x=0$. Its $y$-coordinate is also called the $y$-intercept.",
